NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework-agnostic headless client for managing chat state and streaming."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For typed headless chat UI types and selectors, import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client/ui"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../ui/custom-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom Chat UI Adapters"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-client\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"registerwebmcptools-tools-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"registerWebMCPTools(tools, options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expose executable client tools through the browser WebMCP API. Abort the required signal to remove all tools from this registration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a complete setup and behavior guide, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/webmcp","children":[{"type":"text","value":"WebMCP Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  registerWebMCPTools,\n  type RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { searchProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst controller = new AbortController();\nconst tools = [searchProducts];\nconst options: RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<typeof tools> = {\n  signal: controller.signal,\n  toolOptions: {\n    searchProducts: {\n      title: \"Search products\",\n      annotations: { readOnlyHint: true },\n    },\n  },\n};\n\nawait registerWebMCPTools(tools, options);\n\n// Remove these tools when their owner is no longer active.\ncontroller.abort();","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise<void>"},{"type":"text","value":". It resolves without registration during server rendering, in an insecure context, or when WebMCP is unavailable."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It validates Standard Schema inputs and outputs. A tool with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval: true"},{"type":"text","value":" causes registration to fail."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"public-option-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Public option types"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<TTools, TContext>"},{"type":"text","value":" - Requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal"},{"type":"text","value":". It also contains "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" and the client tool runtime "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WebMCPToolOptionsByName<TTools>"},{"type":"text","value":" - A partial options map keyed by the inferred tool names."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WebMCPToolOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" - Contains the optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"title"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"annotations"},{"type":"text","value":" fields for one tool."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WebMCPToolAnnotations"},{"type":"text","value":" - Contains the optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readOnlyHint"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"untrustedContentHint"},{"type":"text","value":" fields."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context"},{"type":"text","value":" is required when a tool declares a required runtime context. If registration fails, the function removes tools that it registered during the call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"chatclient","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The main client class for managing chat state."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  ChatClient,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type UIMessage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { myClientTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  initialMessages: [],\n  tools: [myClientTool],\n  onMessagesChange: (messages: UIMessage[]) => {\n    console.log(\"Messages updated:\", messages);\n  },\n});\n\n// A new client is IDLE. Attach it when your view appears, detach when it goes.\nclient.attach();","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"lifecycle-attach-and-detach","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attach()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detach()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One page can hold many chats. A browser allows only about six connections to one\norigin, and a chat that is tailing a run holds one for as long as that run lasts. If\nevery chat held a connection, a handful of open views would use every slot and every\nother request would queue behind them, including the request that loads your messages."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"So the connection follows the view. A new client holds none, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attach()"},{"type":"text","value":" starts it, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detach()"},{"type":"text","value":" stops it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you use a framework package ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-vue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-solid"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-svelte"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-preact"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-angular"},{"type":"text","value":"), the hook already does this: it attaches when its view mounts\nand detaches when it unmounts. Call these yourself only when you use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient"},{"type":"text","value":"\ndirectly."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { ChatClient, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  threadId: \"thread-1\",\n  persistence: true,\n});\n\nclient.attach(); // start: rejoin a run in progress, and load the thread\nclient.detach(); // stop: drop the connection, keep messages and the run pointer","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What each one guarantees:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attach()"},{"type":"text","value":" is safe to call more than once. Attaching an attached client does nothing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detach()"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps the transcript, the resume pointer and the run id. The run keeps\ngoing on the server while nobody watches, so re-attaching repaints at once and picks\nit back up from the durable log."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detach()"},{"type":"text","value":" is neither "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":" (which ends the run) nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dispose()"},{"type":"text","value":" (which ends the\nclient). It says only that no view is watching right now."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A chat with no persistence has no resume pointer and no stored thread, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attach()"},{"type":"text","value":"\nissues no request at all."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"migrating-from-constructor-tailing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Migrating from constructor tailing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Earlier versions started tailing inside the constructor. If you build a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient"},{"type":"text","value":"\nyourself, add "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client.attach()"},{"type":"text","value":" where your view appears and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"client.detach()"},{"type":"text","value":" where it\ngoes away. Users of the framework hooks need no change."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"constructor-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Constructor Options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"connection"},{"type":"text","value":" - Connection adapter for streaming"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialMessages?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Initial messages array"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"threadId?"},{"type":"text","value":" - The only identity for this chat. Required when persistence is on. If omitted, minted after mount."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Arbitrary client-controlled JSON forwarded to the server in the AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RunAgentInput.forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" field"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body?"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" instead. Still works — values are merged into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" on the wire and mirrored under the legacy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" field for backward compatibility"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Optional BYOK keyring from "},{"type":"link","href":"#definebyok","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineByok"}]},{"type":"text","value":". On each send the client prepares the resolved provider and stamps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-*"},{"type":"text","value":" request headers. Keys never go in the body"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byokProvider?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Optional function that returns the provider slug for this chat. If it returns a slug, only that key is prepared and sent. Otherwise the merged "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provider"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":", and per-call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" is used. Later sources win. If no slug resolves, the send throws instead of attaching every stored key"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"context?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Typed client-local runtime context passed to client tool implementations. This value is not serialized to the server"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Registered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".client()"},{"type":"text","value":" tool implementations. The client automatically executes matching tools when the model calls them"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onResponse?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when response is received"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onChunk?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when stream chunk is received"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFinish?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when response finishes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onError?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when error occurs"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onInterruptStateChange?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when interrupt state changes; context source is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":" for restored state and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live"},{"type":"text","value":" for streamed or client-initiated updates"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMessagesChange?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when messages change"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onLoadingChange?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when loading state changes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onHydratingChange?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when the client starts or stops loading the chat from persistence"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onErrorChange?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Callback when error state changes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streamProcessor?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Stream processing configuration"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"methods","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methods"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"sendmessage-content-string-multimodalcontent-body-sendoptions","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage(content: string | MultimodalContent, body?, sendOptions?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sends a user message and starts the run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MultimodalContent"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ content, id?, metadata? }"},{"type":"text","value":". The string form has no metadata. Pass the object form to stamp "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" on the user "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIMessage"},{"type":"text","value":". TanStack writes the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":" key. Your keys stay at the top of the bag."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The second argument is extra JSON merged into this request's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":". The third argument is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SendMessageOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ whenBusy }"},{"type":"text","value":" overrides the queue policy for this send. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ body }"},{"type":"text","value":" is extra JSON too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat-level "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":", the positional argument, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendOptions.body"},{"type":"text","value":" shallow-merge. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendOptions.body"},{"type":"text","value":" wins on key collisions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Framework hooks expose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage(content, sendOptions)"},{"type":"text","value":" with no positional body. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ body }"},{"type":"text","value":" there. It merges with the hook's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" the same way."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.sendMessage(\"Hello!\");\n\nawait client.sendMessage({\n  content: \"Show me failed logins\",\n  metadata: { author: { id: \"user-42\", name: \"Dana\" } },\n});\n\nawait client.sendMessage(\"Summarize the attached files\", undefined, {\n  body: { attachmentIds: [\"att_1\", \"att_2\"] },\n  whenBusy: \"interrupt\",\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your server reads the merged JSON from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chatParamsFromRequest"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, forwardedProps } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n  if (\n    forwardedProps &&\n    typeof forwardedProps === \"object\" &&\n    \"attachmentIds\" in forwardedProps\n  ) {\n    const { attachmentIds } = forwardedProps;\n    if (Array.isArray(attachmentIds) && attachmentIds.length > 0) {\n      // Look up the uploads. Do not add them to `messages`.\n    }\n  }\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"append-message-modelmessage-uimessage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"append(message: ModelMessage | UIMessage)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Appends a message to the conversation. If you pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIMessage"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"append"},{"type":"text","value":" copies "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"uiMessage.metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" onto the stored message."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"append()"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves after the full HTTP response is processed when this call starts the stream. If a stream is already in progress, this call queues the send and the returned promise can resolve before that queued response is processed. A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"RUN_FINISHED"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"finishReason: \"tool_calls\""},{"type":"text","value":" does not end the wait when the agent loop continues in that response."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { client } from \"./client\";\nimport type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nawait client.append({\n  role: \"user\",\n  content: \"Additional context\",\n});\n\nconst stamped: UIMessage = {\n  id: \"user-1\",\n  role: \"user\",\n  parts: [{ type: \"text\", content: \"Show me failed logins\" }],\n  metadata: { author: { id: \"user-42\", name: \"Dana\" } },\n};\nawait client.append(stamped);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"reload","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reload()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reloads the last assistant message."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.reload();","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"attach","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attach()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start tailing. Rejoins a run that is still in progress and, in server-authoritative\nmode, loads the stored thread. Idempotent. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#lifecycle-attach-and-detach","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"detach","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"detach()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stop tailing and drop the connection. Keeps messages, the run pointer and the run\nid, so a later "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"attach()"},{"type":"text","value":" continues where it left off. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"#lifecycle-attach-and-detach","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"stop","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stops the current response generation. It aborts the in-flight request.\nPending client-tool results for that turn are ignored. A later\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolResult()"},{"type":"text","value":" call for that turn is ignored. It does not start a resume."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { client } from \"./client\";\n\nclient.stop();","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"clear","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clear()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clears all messages."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { client } from \"./client\";\n\nclient.clear();","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"setmessagesmanually-messages-uimessage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setMessagesManually(messages: UIMessage[])"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manually sets the messages array."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { client } from \"./client\";\nimport type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst newMessages: UIMessage[] = [];\nclient.setMessagesManually([...newMessages]);","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"addtoolresult-result","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolResult(result)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adds the result of a client-side tool execution. After "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stop()"},{"type":"text","value":", a result for\nthe stopped turn is ignored. A new user message starts a new turn. Then\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolResult()"},{"type":"text","value":" applies to that turn."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.addToolResult({\n  toolCallId: \"call_123\",\n  tool: \"toolName\",\n  output: { result: \"...\" },\n  state: \"output-available\",\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"addtoolapprovalresponse-response","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"addToolApprovalResponse(response)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responds to a tool approval request."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.addToolApprovalResponse({\n  id: \"approval_123\",\n  approved: true,\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"properties","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Properties"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"messages: UIMessage[]"},{"type":"text","value":" - Current messages"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isLoading: boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" - Whether a response is being generated"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isHydrating: boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" - Whether the chat is loading from persistence. Read it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getIsHydrating()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error: Error | undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" - Current error, if any"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"connection-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Connection Adapters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a complete transport walkthrough, see\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../transports/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transports"}]},{"type":"text","value":". For React Native and Expo,\nsee "},{"type":"link","href":"../transports/react-native","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Native"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start-react-native","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick Start: React Native"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fetchserversentevents-url-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchServerSentEvents(url, options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an SSE connection adapter."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\", {\n  headers: {\n    Authorization: \"Bearer token\",\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fetchhttpstream-url-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream(url, options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a newline-delimited JSON HTTP stream connection adapter. Pair it with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchHttpStream(\"/api/chat\");","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":" requires a runtime with streaming "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response.body.getReader()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextDecoder"},{"type":"text","value":". If the runtime cannot expose an\nincremental response body, it throws "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UnsupportedResponseStreamError"},{"type":"text","value":"; use the\nXHR adapters in React Native or Expo."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fetchjson-url-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchJson(url, options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a connection adapter for one JSON body per request. Pair it with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toJsonResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server. It does not need a streaming response body."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchJson } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchJson(\"/api/chat\", {\n  pollIntervalMs: 500,\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It takes the fetch adapter options, plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pollIntervalMs"},{"type":"text","value":" (default 250). When a\nreply has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"done: false"},{"type":"text","value":", the adapter waits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pollIntervalMs"},{"type":"text","value":" and sends\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET ?runId=<id>&offset=<offset>"},{"type":"text","value":". Serve that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"resumeJsonResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":".\nSee "},{"type":"link","href":"../transports/json","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"xhrhttpstream-url-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrHttpStream(url, options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XMLHttpRequest"},{"type":"text","value":"-backed newline-delimited JSON stream adapter. This\nis the recommended default for React Native and Expo chat screens. Pair it with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { xhrHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = xhrHttpStream(\"http://192.168.1.10:8787/chat/http\", {\n  headers: { Authorization: \"Bearer token\" },\n  withCredentials: true,\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"xhrserversentevents-url-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrServerSentEvents(url, options?)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"XMLHttpRequest"},{"type":"text","value":"-backed SSE adapter for runtimes where XHR progress\nevents are more reliable than streaming "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":". Pair it with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { xhrServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = xhrServerSentEvents(\"http://192.168.1.10:8787/chat/sse\");","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"adapter-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fetch adapters accept:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers?: Record<string, string> | Headers"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"credentials?: RequestCredentials"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal?: AbortSignal"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body?: Record<string, any>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchClient?: typeof globalThis.fetch"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"XHR adapters accept:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers?: Record<string, string> | Headers"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withCredentials?: boolean"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"signal?: AbortSignal"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body?: Record<string, any>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrFactory?: () => XMLHttpRequest"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" is merged into the AG-UI "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" payload. Values from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" on the client and per-message "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendMessage"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" (positional\nor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sendOptions.body"},{"type":"text","value":") override static adapter "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"body"},{"type":"text","value":" values."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"stream-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream errors"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UnsupportedResponseStreamError"},{"type":"text","value":" - thrown by fetch-based adapters when\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response.body"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response.body.getReader()"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextDecoder"},{"type":"text","value":" is missing."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StreamTruncatedError"},{"type":"text","value":" - thrown when an SSE or NDJSON stream ends with\nunterminated trailing data, usually because the server, proxy, or network cut\nthe connection mid-line."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"stream-connectfn","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stream(connectFn)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a custom connection adapter."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { stream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = stream(async (messages, data, signal) => {\n  // `data` here carries the merged forwardedProps. The fetch-based\n  // adapters serialize it as the AG-UI `RunAgentInput.forwardedProps`\n  // field on the wire (with a backward-compat `data` mirror).\n  const response = await fetch(\"/api/chat\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    body: JSON.stringify({ messages, forwardedProps: data }),\n    signal,\n  });\n  return processStream(response);\n});","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"helper-functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helper Functions"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"clienttools-tools","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientTools(...tools)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional."}]},{"type":"text","value":" A plain array — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools: [tool1, tool2]"},{"type":"text","value":" — already narrows tool names, inputs and outputs without any wrapper or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"as const"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientTools()"},{"type":"text","value":" is an identity helper that performs the same capture explicitly; reach for it only when you want to build a shared, reusable tools tuple outside the hook/options call."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  clientTools,\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type UIMessage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst messages: UIMessage[] = [];\n\nconst myTool1 = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"myTool1\",\n  description: \"First tool\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ result: z.string() }),\n});\n\nconst myTool2 = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"myTool2\",\n  description: \"Second tool\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ result: z.string() }),\n});\n\n// Create client implementations\nconst tool1Client = myTool1.client((input) => {\n  // Implementation\n  return { result: input.query };\n});\n\nconst tool2Client = myTool2.client((input) => {\n  // Implementation\n  return { result: input.query };\n});\n\n// The explicit-capture form (equivalent to `[tool1Client, tool2Client]`).\nconst tools = clientTools(tool1Client, tool2Client);\n\n// Now when you use these tools in chat options:\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools, // Fully typed with literal tool names\n});\n\n// In your component:\nmessages.forEach((message) => {\n  message.parts.forEach((part) => {\n    if (part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.name === \"myTool1\") {\n      // ✅ TypeScript knows part.name is literally \"myTool1\"\n      // ✅ part.input is typed from myTool1's input schema\n      // ✅ part.output is typed from myTool1's output schema\n    }\n  });\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"createchatclientoptions-options","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatClientOptions(options)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helper function to create typed chat client options with proper type inference."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { tool1, tool2 } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst tools = [tool1, tool2];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\n// Use InferChatMessages to extract message types\ntype ChatMessages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatClientOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" also preserves typed client runtime context:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\ntype ClientContext = {\n  activeProjectId: string;\n};\n\nconst projectTool = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"projectAction\",\n  description: \"Run a project action\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ action: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ ok: z.boolean() }),\n});\n\nconst tool = projectTool.client<ClientContext>((input, ctx: { context: ClientContext }) => {\n  console.log(ctx.context.activeProjectId, input.action);\n  return { ok: true };\n});\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools: [tool],\n  context: {\n    activeProjectId: \"project_123\",\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client runtime context is local to the client instance. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"forwardedProps"},{"type":"text","value":" for explicit client-to-server handoff of serializable values, then validate and map those values into server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({ context })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"definebyok","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defineByok"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Factory for a headless BYOK keyring. Import it from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client/byok"},{"type":"text","value":". Pass the instance into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChatClient"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":", or a generation hook. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a full client and relay walkthrough."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client/byok\";\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"factory-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Factory options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"storage?"},{"type":"text","value":" - A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyringStorage"},{"type":"text","value":" implementation. Default is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStorage()"},{"type":"text","value":" (session only, not saved)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"providers?"},{"type":"text","value":" - Descriptors whose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"with"},{"type":"text","value":" companions the store expands. With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[cloudflareByok, cloudflareAccountByok]"},{"type":"text","value":", a send for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cloudflare"},{"type":"text","value":" carries the token and the account id headers, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prepare"},{"type":"text","value":" prompts for each missing one"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"methods-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Methods"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update(provider, key)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Persist a key for a provider slug ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}"},{"type":"text","value":"), then update the snapshot. Throws if the id is not a slug, the key is empty, or storage fails"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update(key)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Persist a key for the current "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" provider. Throws if "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" is null"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clear(provider?)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Persist the removal, then drop one key, or all keys when you omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provider"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unlock()"},{"type":"text","value":" - Decrypt unlockable storage (passkey). No-op for memory storage"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"headers(provider)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-*"},{"type":"text","value":" headers for that slug and its companions. Chat and generation clients throw if no slug resolves — they do not send every stored key"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prepare(provider?)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Wait for hydration, then unlock if needed. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provider"},{"type":"text","value":" is set and the key for it or a companion is empty with no server coverage, throw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ByokBlockedError"},{"type":"text","value":" and set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" for that slug"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ready()"},{"type":"text","value":" - Resolve when constructor hydration (peek/load) finishes"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"setServerCoverage(flags)"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":" means do not block a send when the browser has no key (the relay can fill from env). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" restores the default: block. A record merges per-slug flags"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"request(provider, reason)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"prompt"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ provider, reason }"},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"missing"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"locked"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"invalid"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSnapshot()"},{"type":"text","value":" - Return the current "},{"type":"link","href":"#snapshot","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ByokSnapshot"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribe(listener)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"listener"},{"type":"text","value":" on each change. Returns an unsubscribe function"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keys()"},{"type":"text","value":" - Return a copy of the raw keyring. Do not render this in the UI"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"snapshot","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Snapshot"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getSnapshot()"},{"type":"text","value":" (and framework readers such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useByok"},{"type":"text","value":") return:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type ByokSnapshot = {\n  status: Partial<Record<string, KeyStatus>>;\n  locked: boolean;\n  prompt: { provider: string; reason: \"missing\" | \"locked\" | \"invalid\" } | null;\n  storageError: string | null;\n};\n\ntype KeyStatus =\n  | { state: \"empty\" }\n  | { state: \"set\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"locked\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"validating\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"valid\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"invalid\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"error\"; masked: string; message: string };","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" is sparse: only slugs that have a key, a lock, or a validation result appear. A missing entry means no key. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"masked"},{"type":"text","value":" is the last four characters of the key ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maskKey"},{"type":"text","value":"). Read it with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"masked\" in status"},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ state: \"empty\" }"},{"type":"text","value":" has no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"masked"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"storageError"},{"type":"text","value":" is set when peek/load fails. The snapshot never includes the raw key."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"storage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Storage"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultByokStorage(options?)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Passkey-encrypted IndexedDB when WebAuthn is available in a secure context. Otherwise "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStorage()"},{"type":"text","value":" with a warning. WebAuthn support is not the same as PRF — first save still throws if the authenticator lacks PRF"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryStorage()"},{"type":"text","value":" - In-memory on the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ByokClient"},{"type":"text","value":" instance. This backend does not persist. Keys are gone when the client is dropped or the page reloads"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"passkeyStorage(options?)"},{"type":"text","value":" - Encrypt the keyring with a WebAuthn passkey. First save throws if the authenticator does not support PRF"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyringStorage"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ id, label, persistent, unlockable?, peek?, load, save, clear }"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This library does not ship a dialog. Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"byok.update(provider, value)"},{"type":"text","value":" from your own UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"uimessage","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UIMessage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface UIMessage {\n  id: string;\n  role: \"system\" | \"user\" | \"assistant\";\n  parts: MessagePart[];\n  name?: string;\n  createdAt?: Date;\n  metadata?: Record<string, any>;\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"metadata"},{"type":"text","value":" is an optional AG-UI bag ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, any>"},{"type":"text","value":"). TanStack writes the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tanstack"},{"type":"text","value":" key. Your keys stay at the top."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"messagepart","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"MessagePart"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type MessagePart = TextPart | ThinkingPart | ToolCallPart | ToolResultPart;","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"textpart","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextPart"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface TextPart {\n  type: \"text\";\n  content: string;\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"thinkingpart","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ThinkingPart"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ThinkingPart {\n  type: \"thinking\";\n  content: string;\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thinking parts represent the model's internal reasoning process. They are typically displayed in a collapsible format and automatically collapse when the response text appears. Thinking parts are UI-only and are not sent back to the model in subsequent requests."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Thinking parts are only available when using models that support reasoning/thinking (e.g., Anthropic Claude with thinking enabled, OpenAI GPT-5 with reasoning enabled)."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toolcallpart","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolCallPart"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ToolCallPart {\n  type: \"tool-call\";\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  arguments: string; // JSON string (may be incomplete during streaming)\n  input?: any; // Parsed tool input (typed from tool's inputSchema)\n  state: ToolCallState;\n  approval?: ApprovalRequest; // only on tools declared `needsApproval: true`\n  output?: any; // Tool execution output (typed from tool's outputSchema)\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you pass a typed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools"},{"type":"text","value":" array (a plain array works — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientTools()"},{"type":"text","value":" is optional), the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"output"},{"type":"text","value":" fields are automatically typed based on your tool's Zod schemas, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"name"},{"type":"text","value":" becomes a discriminated union enabling type narrowing. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"approval"},{"type":"text","value":" field is present "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"only"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on parts for tools declared with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval: true"},{"type":"text","value":" — narrow by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"part.name"},{"type":"text","value":" (or guard with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'approval' in part"},{"type":"text","value":") before accessing it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toolresultpart","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolResultPart"}]},{"type":"code","value":"interface ToolResultPart {\n  type: \"tool-result\";\n  id?: string;\n  name?: string;\n  toolCallId: string;\n  content: string | ContentPart[];\n  state: ToolResultState;\n  error?: string;\n  metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;\n  createdAt?: Date;\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toolcallstate","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolCallState"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type ToolCallState =\n  | \"awaiting-input\"\n  | \"input-streaming\"\n  | \"input-complete\"\n  | \"approval-requested\"\n  | \"approval-responded\"\n  | \"complete\";","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"toolresultstate","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ToolResultState"}]},{"type":"code","value":"type ToolResultState =\n  | \"streaming\"\n  | \"complete\"\n  | \"error\";","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"stream-processing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stream Processing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configure stream processing with chunk strategies:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  ChatClient,\n  ImmediateStrategy,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  streamProcessor: {\n    chunkStrategy: new ImmediateStrategy(), // Emit every chunk\n  },\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Getting Started"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn the basics"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/byok","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bring Your Own Key"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Store keys in the browser and send "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x-byok-*"},{"type":"text","value":" headers"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../transports/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Transports"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Learn about adapters"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./ai-react","children":[{"type":"text","value":"@tanstack/ai-react API"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - React hooks wrapper"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"registerwebmcptools-tools-options","text":"registerWebMCPTools(tools, options)","level":2},{"id":"public-option-types","text":"Public option types","level":3},{"id":"chatclient","text":"ChatClient","level":2},{"id":"lifecycle-attach-and-detach","text":"Lifecycle: attach() and detach()","level":3},{"id":"migrating-from-constructor-tailing","text":"Migrating from constructor tailing","level":4},{"id":"constructor-options","text":"Constructor Options","level":3},{"id":"methods","text":"Methods","level":3},{"id":"sendmessage-content-string-multimodalcontent-body-sendoptions","text":"sendMessage(content: string | MultimodalContent, body?, sendOptions?)","level":4},{"id":"append-message-modelmessage-uimessage","text":"append(message: ModelMessage | UIMessage)","level":4},{"id":"reload","text":"reload()","level":4},{"id":"attach","text":"attach()","level":4},{"id":"detach","text":"detach()","level":4},{"id":"stop","text":"stop()","level":4},{"id":"clear","text":"clear()","level":4},{"id":"setmessagesmanually-messages-uimessage","text":"setMessagesManually(messages: UIMessage[])","level":4},{"id":"addtoolresult-result","text":"addToolResult(result)","level":4},{"id":"addtoolapprovalresponse-response","text":"addToolApprovalResponse(response)","level":4},{"id":"properties","text":"Properties","level":3},{"id":"connection-adapters","text":"Connection Adapters","level":2},{"id":"fetchserversentevents-url-options","text":"fetchServerSentEvents(url, options?)","level":3},{"id":"fetchhttpstream-url-options","text":"fetchHttpStream(url, options?)","level":3},{"id":"fetchjson-url-options","text":"fetchJson(url, options?)","level":3},{"id":"xhrhttpstream-url-options","text":"xhrHttpStream(url, options?)","level":3},{"id":"xhrserversentevents-url-options","text":"xhrServerSentEvents(url, options?)","level":3},{"id":"adapter-options","text":"Adapter options","level":3},{"id":"stream-errors","text":"Stream errors","level":3},{"id":"stream-connectfn","text":"stream(connectFn)","level":3},{"id":"helper-functions","text":"Helper Functions","level":2},{"id":"clienttools-tools","text":"clientTools(...tools)","level":3},{"id":"createchatclientoptions-options","text":"createChatClientOptions(options)","level":3},{"id":"definebyok","text":"defineByok","level":2},{"id":"factory-options","text":"Factory options","level":3},{"id":"methods-2","text":"Methods","level":3},{"id":"snapshot","text":"Snapshot","level":3},{"id":"storage","text":"Storage","level":3},{"id":"types","text":"Types","level":2},{"id":"uimessage","text":"UIMessage","level":3},{"id":"messagepart","text":"MessagePart","level":3},{"id":"textpart","text":"TextPart","level":3},{"id":"thinkingpart","text":"ThinkingPart","level":3},{"id":"toolcallpart","text":"ToolCallPart","level":3},{"id":"toolresultpart","text":"ToolResultPart","level":3},{"id":"toolcallstate","text":"ToolCallState","level":3},{"id":"toolresultstate","text":"ToolResultState","level":3},{"id":"stream-processing","text":"Stream Processing","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nFramework-agnostic headless client for managing chat state and streaming.\n\nFor typed headless chat UI types and selectors, import `@tanstack/ai-client/ui`. See [Custom Chat UI Adapters](../ui/custom-adapters).\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-client\nvue: @tanstack/ai-client\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-client\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-client\npreact: @tanstack/ai-client\nangular: @tanstack/ai-client\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-client\noctane: @tanstack/ai-client\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## `registerWebMCPTools(tools, options)`\n\nExpose executable client tools through the browser WebMCP API. Abort the required signal to remove all tools from this registration.\n\nFor a complete setup and behavior guide, see [WebMCP Tools](../tools/webmcp).\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  registerWebMCPTools,\n  type RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { searchProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst controller = new AbortController();\nconst tools = [searchProducts];\nconst options: RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<typeof tools> = {\n  signal: controller.signal,\n  toolOptions: {\n    searchProducts: {\n      title: \"Search products\",\n      annotations: { readOnlyHint: true },\n    },\n  },\n};\n\nawait registerWebMCPTools(tools, options);\n\n// Remove these tools when their owner is no longer active.\ncontroller.abort();\n```\n\nThe function returns `Promise<void>`. It resolves without registration during server rendering, in an insecure context, or when WebMCP is unavailable.\n\nIt validates Standard Schema inputs and outputs. A tool with `needsApproval: true` causes registration to fail.\n\n### Public option types\n\n- `RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<TTools, TContext>` - Requires `signal`. It also contains `toolOptions` and the client tool runtime `context`.\n- `WebMCPToolOptionsByName<TTools>` - A partial options map keyed by the inferred tool names.\n- `WebMCPToolOptions` - Contains the optional `title` and `annotations` fields for one tool.\n- `WebMCPToolAnnotations` - Contains the optional `readOnlyHint` and `untrustedContentHint` fields.\n\n`context` is required when a tool declares a required runtime context. If registration fails, the function removes tools that it registered during the call.\n\n## `ChatClient`\n\nThe main client class for managing chat state.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  ChatClient,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type UIMessage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { myClientTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  initialMessages: [],\n  tools: [myClientTool],\n  onMessagesChange: (messages: UIMessage[]) => {\n    console.log(\"Messages updated:\", messages);\n  },\n});\n\n// A new client is IDLE. Attach it when your view appears, detach when it goes.\nclient.attach();\n```\n\n### Lifecycle: `attach()` and `detach()`\n\nOne page can hold many chats. A browser allows only about six connections to one\norigin, and a chat that is tailing a run holds one for as long as that run lasts. If\nevery chat held a connection, a handful of open views would use every slot and every\nother request would queue behind them, including the request that loads your messages.\n\nSo the connection follows the view. A new client holds none, `attach()` starts it, and\n`detach()` stops it.\n\nIf you use a framework package (`@tanstack/ai-react`, `-vue`, `-solid`, `-svelte`,\n`-preact`, `-angular`), the hook already does this: it attaches when its view mounts\nand detaches when it unmounts. Call these yourself only when you use `ChatClient`\ndirectly.\n\n```typescript\nimport { ChatClient, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  threadId: \"thread-1\",\n  persistence: true,\n});\n\nclient.attach(); // start: rejoin a run in progress, and load the thread\nclient.detach(); // stop: drop the connection, keep messages and the run pointer\n```\n\nWhat each one guarantees:\n\n- `attach()` is safe to call more than once. Attaching an attached client does nothing.\n- `detach()` keeps the transcript, the resume pointer and the run id. The run keeps\n  going on the server while nobody watches, so re-attaching repaints at once and picks\n  it back up from the durable log.\n- `detach()` is neither `stop()` (which ends the run) nor `dispose()` (which ends the\n  client). It says only that no view is watching right now.\n- A chat with no persistence has no resume pointer and no stored thread, so `attach()`\n  issues no request at all.\n\n#### Migrating from constructor tailing\n\nEarlier versions started tailing inside the constructor. If you build a `ChatClient`\nyourself, add `client.attach()` where your view appears and `client.detach()` where it\ngoes away. Users of the framework hooks need no change.\n\n### Constructor Options\n\n- `connection` - Connection adapter for streaming\n- `initialMessages?` - Initial messages array\n- `threadId?` - The only identity for this chat. Required when persistence is on. If omitted, minted after mount.\n- `forwardedProps?` - Arbitrary client-controlled JSON forwarded to the server in the AG-UI `RunAgentInput.forwardedProps` field\n- `body?` - **Deprecated.** Use `forwardedProps` instead. Still works — values are merged into `forwardedProps` on the wire and mirrored under the legacy `data` field for backward compatibility\n- `byok?` - Optional BYOK keyring from [`defineByok`](#definebyok). On each send the client prepares the resolved provider and stamps `x-byok-*` request headers. Keys never go in the body\n- `byokProvider?` - Optional function that returns the provider slug for this chat. If it returns a slug, only that key is prepared and sent. Otherwise the merged `provider` from `forwardedProps`, `body`, and per-call `sendMessage` `body` is used. Later sources win. If no slug resolves, the send throws instead of attaching every stored key\n- `context?` - Typed client-local runtime context passed to client tool implementations. This value is not serialized to the server\n- `tools?` - Registered `.client()` tool implementations. The client automatically executes matching tools when the model calls them\n- `onResponse?` - Callback when response is received\n- `onChunk?` - Callback when stream chunk is received\n- `onFinish?` - Callback when response finishes\n- `onError?` - Callback when error occurs\n- `onInterruptStateChange?` - Callback when interrupt state changes; context source is `hydrate` for restored state and `live` for streamed or client-initiated updates\n- `onMessagesChange?` - Callback when messages change\n- `onLoadingChange?` - Callback when loading state changes\n- `onHydratingChange?` - Callback when the client starts or stops loading the chat from persistence\n- `onErrorChange?` - Callback when error state changes\n- `streamProcessor?` - Stream processing configuration\n\n### Methods\n\n#### `sendMessage(content: string | MultimodalContent, body?, sendOptions?)`\n\nSends a user message and starts the run.\n\n`MultimodalContent` is `{ content, id?, metadata? }`. The string form has no metadata. Pass the object form to stamp `metadata` on the user `UIMessage`. TanStack writes the `tanstack` key. Your keys stay at the top of the bag.\n\nThe second argument is extra JSON merged into this request's `forwardedProps`. The third argument is `SendMessageOptions`. `{ whenBusy }` overrides the queue policy for this send. `{ body }` is extra JSON too.\n\nChat-level `body`, the positional argument, and `sendOptions.body` shallow-merge. `sendOptions.body` wins on key collisions.\n\nFramework hooks expose `sendMessage(content, sendOptions)` with no positional body. Pass `{ body }` there. It merges with the hook's `body` the same way.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.sendMessage(\"Hello!\");\n\nawait client.sendMessage({\n  content: \"Show me failed logins\",\n  metadata: { author: { id: \"user-42\", name: \"Dana\" } },\n});\n\nawait client.sendMessage(\"Summarize the attached files\", undefined, {\n  body: { attachmentIds: [\"att_1\", \"att_2\"] },\n  whenBusy: \"interrupt\",\n});\n```\n\nYour server reads the merged JSON from `chatParamsFromRequest`:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, forwardedProps } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n  if (\n    forwardedProps &&\n    typeof forwardedProps === \"object\" &&\n    \"attachmentIds\" in forwardedProps\n  ) {\n    const { attachmentIds } = forwardedProps;\n    if (Array.isArray(attachmentIds) && attachmentIds.length > 0) {\n      // Look up the uploads. Do not add them to `messages`.\n    }\n  }\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n#### `append(message: ModelMessage | UIMessage)`\n\nAppends a message to the conversation. If you pass a `UIMessage`, `append` copies `uiMessage.metadata` onto the stored message.\n\n`append()` resolves after the full HTTP response is processed when this call starts the stream. If a stream is already in progress, this call queues the send and the returned promise can resolve before that queued response is processed. A `RUN_FINISHED` with `finishReason: \"tool_calls\"` does not end the wait when the agent loop continues in that response.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\nimport type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nawait client.append({\n  role: \"user\",\n  content: \"Additional context\",\n});\n\nconst stamped: UIMessage = {\n  id: \"user-1\",\n  role: \"user\",\n  parts: [{ type: \"text\", content: \"Show me failed logins\" }],\n  metadata: { author: { id: \"user-42\", name: \"Dana\" } },\n};\nawait client.append(stamped);\n```\n\n#### `reload()`\n\nReloads the last assistant message.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.reload();\n```\n\n#### `attach()`\n\nStart tailing. Rejoins a run that is still in progress and, in server-authoritative\nmode, loads the stored thread. Idempotent. See\n[Lifecycle](#lifecycle-attach-and-detach).\n\n#### `detach()`\n\nStop tailing and drop the connection. Keeps messages, the run pointer and the run\nid, so a later `attach()` continues where it left off. See\n[Lifecycle](#lifecycle-attach-and-detach).\n\n#### `stop()`\n\nStops the current response generation. It aborts the in-flight request.\nPending client-tool results for that turn are ignored. A later\n`addToolResult()` call for that turn is ignored. It does not start a resume.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nclient.stop();\n```\n\n#### `clear()`\n\nClears all messages.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nclient.clear();\n```\n\n#### `setMessagesManually(messages: UIMessage[])`\n\nManually sets the messages array.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\nimport type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst newMessages: UIMessage[] = [];\nclient.setMessagesManually([...newMessages]);\n```\n\n#### `addToolResult(result)`\n\nAdds the result of a client-side tool execution. After `stop()`, a result for\nthe stopped turn is ignored. A new user message starts a new turn. Then\n`addToolResult()` applies to that turn.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.addToolResult({\n  toolCallId: \"call_123\",\n  tool: \"toolName\",\n  output: { result: \"...\" },\n  state: \"output-available\",\n});\n```\n\n#### `addToolApprovalResponse(response)`\n\nResponds to a tool approval request.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.addToolApprovalResponse({\n  id: \"approval_123\",\n  approved: true,\n});\n```\n\n### Properties\n\n- `messages: UIMessage[]` - Current messages\n- `isLoading: boolean` - Whether a response is being generated\n- `isHydrating: boolean` - Whether the chat is loading from persistence. Read it with `getIsHydrating()`\n- `error: Error | undefined` - Current error, if any\n\n## Connection Adapters\n\nFor a complete transport walkthrough, see\n[Transports](../transports/overview). For React Native and Expo,\nsee [React Native](../transports/react-native) and\n[Quick Start: React Native](../getting-started/quick-start-react-native).\n\n### `fetchServerSentEvents(url, options?)`\n\nCreates an SSE connection adapter.\n\n```typescript\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\", {\n  headers: {\n    Authorization: \"Bearer token\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### `fetchHttpStream(url, options?)`\n\nCreates a newline-delimited JSON HTTP stream connection adapter. Pair it with\n`toHttpResponse()` on the server.\n\n```typescript\nimport { fetchHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchHttpStream(\"/api/chat\");\n```\n\n`fetchHttpStream()` requires a runtime with streaming `fetch`,\n`Response.body.getReader()`, and `TextDecoder`. If the runtime cannot expose an\nincremental response body, it throws `UnsupportedResponseStreamError`; use the\nXHR adapters in React Native or Expo.\n\n### `fetchJson(url, options?)`\n\nCreates a connection adapter for one JSON body per request. Pair it with\n`toJsonResponse()` on the server. It does not need a streaming response body.\n\n```typescript\nimport { fetchJson } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchJson(\"/api/chat\", {\n  pollIntervalMs: 500,\n});\n```\n\nIt takes the fetch adapter options, plus `pollIntervalMs` (default 250). When a\nreply has `done: false`, the adapter waits `pollIntervalMs` and sends\n`GET ?runId=<id>&offset=<offset>`. Serve that `GET` with `resumeJsonResponse()`.\nSee [JSON](../transports/json).\n\n### `xhrHttpStream(url, options?)`\n\nCreates an `XMLHttpRequest`-backed newline-delimited JSON stream adapter. This\nis the recommended default for React Native and Expo chat screens. Pair it with\n`toHttpResponse()` on the server.\n\n```typescript\nimport { xhrHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = xhrHttpStream(\"http://192.168.1.10:8787/chat/http\", {\n  headers: { Authorization: \"Bearer token\" },\n  withCredentials: true,\n});\n```\n\n### `xhrServerSentEvents(url, options?)`\n\nCreates an `XMLHttpRequest`-backed SSE adapter for runtimes where XHR progress\nevents are more reliable than streaming `fetch`. Pair it with\n`toServerSentEventsResponse()` on the server.\n\n```typescript\nimport { xhrServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = xhrServerSentEvents(\"http://192.168.1.10:8787/chat/sse\");\n```\n\n### Adapter options\n\nFetch adapters accept:\n\n- `headers?: Record<string, string> | Headers`\n- `credentials?: RequestCredentials`\n- `signal?: AbortSignal`\n- `body?: Record<string, any>`\n- `fetchClient?: typeof globalThis.fetch`\n\nXHR adapters accept:\n\n- `headers?: Record<string, string> | Headers`\n- `withCredentials?: boolean`\n- `signal?: AbortSignal`\n- `body?: Record<string, any>`\n- `xhrFactory?: () => XMLHttpRequest`\n\n`body` is merged into the AG-UI `forwardedProps` payload. Values from\n`forwardedProps` on the client and per-message `sendMessage` `body` (positional\nor `sendOptions.body`) override static adapter `body` values.\n\n### Stream errors\n\n- `UnsupportedResponseStreamError` - thrown by fetch-based adapters when\n  `Response.body`, `Response.body.getReader()`, or `TextDecoder` is missing.\n- `StreamTruncatedError` - thrown when an SSE or NDJSON stream ends with\n  unterminated trailing data, usually because the server, proxy, or network cut\n  the connection mid-line.\n\n### `stream(connectFn)`\n\nCreates a custom connection adapter.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { stream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = stream(async (messages, data, signal) => {\n  // `data` here carries the merged forwardedProps. The fetch-based\n  // adapters serialize it as the AG-UI `RunAgentInput.forwardedProps`\n  // field on the wire (with a backward-compat `data` mirror).\n  const response = await fetch(\"/api/chat\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    body: JSON.stringify({ messages, forwardedProps: data }),\n    signal,\n  });\n  return processStream(response);\n});\n```\n\n## Helper Functions\n\n### `clientTools(...tools)`\n\n**Optional.** A plain array — `tools: [tool1, tool2]` — already narrows tool names, inputs and outputs without any wrapper or `as const`. `clientTools()` is an identity helper that performs the same capture explicitly; reach for it only when you want to build a shared, reusable tools tuple outside the hook/options call.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  clientTools,\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type UIMessage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst messages: UIMessage[] = [];\n\nconst myTool1 = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"myTool1\",\n  description: \"First tool\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ result: z.string() }),\n});\n\nconst myTool2 = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"myTool2\",\n  description: \"Second tool\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ result: z.string() }),\n});\n\n// Create client implementations\nconst tool1Client = myTool1.client((input) => {\n  // Implementation\n  return { result: input.query };\n});\n\nconst tool2Client = myTool2.client((input) => {\n  // Implementation\n  return { result: input.query };\n});\n\n// The explicit-capture form (equivalent to `[tool1Client, tool2Client]`).\nconst tools = clientTools(tool1Client, tool2Client);\n\n// Now when you use these tools in chat options:\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools, // Fully typed with literal tool names\n});\n\n// In your component:\nmessages.forEach((message) => {\n  message.parts.forEach((part) => {\n    if (part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.name === \"myTool1\") {\n      // ✅ TypeScript knows part.name is literally \"myTool1\"\n      // ✅ part.input is typed from myTool1's input schema\n      // ✅ part.output is typed from myTool1's output schema\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `createChatClientOptions(options)`\n\nHelper function to create typed chat client options with proper type inference.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { tool1, tool2 } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst tools = [tool1, tool2];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\n// Use InferChatMessages to extract message types\ntype ChatMessages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;\n```\n\n`createChatClientOptions` also preserves typed client runtime context:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\ntype ClientContext = {\n  activeProjectId: string;\n};\n\nconst projectTool = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"projectAction\",\n  description: \"Run a project action\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ action: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ ok: z.boolean() }),\n});\n\nconst tool = projectTool.client<ClientContext>((input, ctx: { context: ClientContext }) => {\n  console.log(ctx.context.activeProjectId, input.action);\n  return { ok: true };\n});\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools: [tool],\n  context: {\n    activeProjectId: \"project_123\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\nClient runtime context is local to the client instance. Use `forwardedProps` for explicit client-to-server handoff of serializable values, then validate and map those values into server `chat({ context })`.\n\n## `defineByok`\n\nFactory for a headless BYOK keyring. Import it from `@tanstack/ai-client/byok`. Pass the instance into `ChatClient`, `useChat`, or a generation hook. See [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) for a full client and relay walkthrough.\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client/byok\";\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n});\n```\n\n### Factory options\n\n- `storage?` - A `KeyringStorage` implementation. Default is `memoryStorage()` (session only, not saved)\n- `providers?` - Descriptors whose `with` companions the store expands. With `[cloudflareByok, cloudflareAccountByok]`, a send for `cloudflare` carries the token and the account id headers, and `prepare` prompts for each missing one\n\n### Methods\n\n- `update(provider, key)` - Persist a key for a provider slug (`[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}`), then update the snapshot. Throws if the id is not a slug, the key is empty, or storage fails\n- `update(key)` - Persist a key for the current `prompt` provider. Throws if `prompt` is null\n- `clear(provider?)` - Persist the removal, then drop one key, or all keys when you omit `provider`\n- `unlock()` - Decrypt unlockable storage (passkey). No-op for memory storage\n- `headers(provider)` - Return `x-byok-*` headers for that slug and its companions. Chat and generation clients throw if no slug resolves — they do not send every stored key\n- `prepare(provider?)` - Wait for hydration, then unlock if needed. If `provider` is set and the key for it or a companion is empty with no server coverage, throw `ByokBlockedError` and set `prompt` for that slug\n- `ready()` - Resolve when constructor hydration (peek/load) finishes\n- `setServerCoverage(flags)` - `true` means do not block a send when the browser has no key (the relay can fill from env). `false` restores the default: block. A record merges per-slug flags\n- `request(provider, reason)` - Set `prompt` to `{ provider, reason }` (`missing` | `locked` | `invalid`)\n- `getSnapshot()` - Return the current [`ByokSnapshot`](#snapshot)\n- `subscribe(listener)` - Call `listener` on each change. Returns an unsubscribe function\n- `keys()` - Return a copy of the raw keyring. Do not render this in the UI\n\n### Snapshot\n\n`getSnapshot()` (and framework readers such as `useByok`) return:\n\n```typescript ignore\ntype ByokSnapshot = {\n  status: Partial<Record<string, KeyStatus>>;\n  locked: boolean;\n  prompt: { provider: string; reason: \"missing\" | \"locked\" | \"invalid\" } | null;\n  storageError: string | null;\n};\n\ntype KeyStatus =\n  | { state: \"empty\" }\n  | { state: \"set\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"locked\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"validating\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"valid\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"invalid\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"error\"; masked: string; message: string };\n```\n\n`status` is sparse: only slugs that have a key, a lock, or a validation result appear. A missing entry means no key. `masked` is the last four characters of the key (`maskKey`). Read it with `\"masked\" in status` — `{ state: \"empty\" }` has no `masked`. `storageError` is set when peek/load fails. The snapshot never includes the raw key.\n\n### Storage\n\n- `defaultByokStorage(options?)` - Passkey-encrypted IndexedDB when WebAuthn is available in a secure context. Otherwise `memoryStorage()` with a warning. WebAuthn support is not the same as PRF — first save still throws if the authenticator lacks PRF\n- `memoryStorage()` - In-memory on the `ByokClient` instance. This backend does not persist. Keys are gone when the client is dropped or the page reloads\n- `passkeyStorage(options?)` - Encrypt the keyring with a WebAuthn passkey. First save throws if the authenticator does not support PRF\n- `KeyringStorage` - `{ id, label, persistent, unlockable?, peek?, load, save, clear }`\n\nThis library does not ship a dialog. Call `byok.update(provider, value)` from your own UI.\n\n## Types\n\n### `UIMessage`\n\n```typescript ignore\ninterface UIMessage {\n  id: string;\n  role: \"system\" | \"user\" | \"assistant\";\n  parts: MessagePart[];\n  name?: string;\n  createdAt?: Date;\n  metadata?: Record<string, any>;\n}\n```\n\n`metadata` is an optional AG-UI bag (`Record<string, any>`). TanStack writes the `tanstack` key. Your keys stay at the top.\n\n### `MessagePart`\n\n```typescript ignore\ntype MessagePart = TextPart | ThinkingPart | ToolCallPart | ToolResultPart;\n```\n\n### `TextPart`\n\n```typescript\ninterface TextPart {\n  type: \"text\";\n  content: string;\n}\n```\n\n### `ThinkingPart`\n\n```typescript\ninterface ThinkingPart {\n  type: \"thinking\";\n  content: string;\n}\n```\n\nThinking parts represent the model's internal reasoning process. They are typically displayed in a collapsible format and automatically collapse when the response text appears. Thinking parts are UI-only and are not sent back to the model in subsequent requests.\n\n**Note:** Thinking parts are only available when using models that support reasoning/thinking (e.g., Anthropic Claude with thinking enabled, OpenAI GPT-5 with reasoning enabled).\n\n### `ToolCallPart`\n\n```typescript ignore\ninterface ToolCallPart {\n  type: \"tool-call\";\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  arguments: string; // JSON string (may be incomplete during streaming)\n  input?: any; // Parsed tool input (typed from tool's inputSchema)\n  state: ToolCallState;\n  approval?: ApprovalRequest; // only on tools declared `needsApproval: true`\n  output?: any; // Tool execution output (typed from tool's outputSchema)\n}\n```\n\nWhen you pass a typed `tools` array (a plain array works — `clientTools()` is optional), the `input` and `output` fields are automatically typed based on your tool's Zod schemas, and `name` becomes a discriminated union enabling type narrowing. The `approval` field is present **only** on parts for tools declared with `needsApproval: true` — narrow by `part.name` (or guard with `'approval' in part`) before accessing it.\n\n### `ToolResultPart`\n\n```typescript ignore\ninterface ToolResultPart {\n  type: \"tool-result\";\n  id?: string;\n  name?: string;\n  toolCallId: string;\n  content: string | ContentPart[];\n  state: ToolResultState;\n  error?: string;\n  metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;\n  createdAt?: Date;\n}\n```\n\n### `ToolCallState`\n\n```typescript ignore\ntype ToolCallState =\n  | \"awaiting-input\"\n  | \"input-streaming\"\n  | \"input-complete\"\n  | \"approval-requested\"\n  | \"approval-responded\"\n  | \"complete\";\n```\n\n### `ToolResultState`\n\n```typescript ignore\ntype ToolResultState =\n  | \"streaming\"\n  | \"complete\"\n  | \"error\";\n```\n\n## Stream Processing\n\nConfigure stream processing with chunk strategies:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  ChatClient,\n  ImmediateStrategy,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  streamProcessor: {\n    chunkStrategy: new ImmediateStrategy(), // Emit every chunk\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) - Store keys in the browser and send `x-byok-*` headers\n- [Transports](../transports/overview) - Learn about adapters\n- [@tanstack/ai-react API](./ai-react) - React hooks wrapper\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: \"@tanstack/ai-client\"\nslug: /api/ai-client\norder: 2\ndescription: \"API reference for @tanstack/ai-client — the framework-agnostic headless client for managing chat state and streaming transports.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - \"@tanstack/ai-client\"\n  - headless client\n  - ChatClient\n  - chat state\n  - connection adapters\n  - api reference\n---\n\nFramework-agnostic headless client for managing chat state and streaming.\n\nFor typed headless chat UI types and selectors, import `@tanstack/ai-client/ui`. See [Custom Chat UI Adapters](../ui/custom-adapters).\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-client\nvue: @tanstack/ai-client\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-client\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-client\npreact: @tanstack/ai-client\nangular: @tanstack/ai-client\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-client\noctane: @tanstack/ai-client\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n## `registerWebMCPTools(tools, options)`\n\nExpose executable client tools through the browser WebMCP API. Abort the required signal to remove all tools from this registration.\n\nFor a complete setup and behavior guide, see [WebMCP Tools](../tools/webmcp).\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  registerWebMCPTools,\n  type RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { searchProducts } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst controller = new AbortController();\nconst tools = [searchProducts];\nconst options: RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<typeof tools> = {\n  signal: controller.signal,\n  toolOptions: {\n    searchProducts: {\n      title: \"Search products\",\n      annotations: { readOnlyHint: true },\n    },\n  },\n};\n\nawait registerWebMCPTools(tools, options);\n\n// Remove these tools when their owner is no longer active.\ncontroller.abort();\n```\n\nThe function returns `Promise<void>`. It resolves without registration during server rendering, in an insecure context, or when WebMCP is unavailable.\n\nIt validates Standard Schema inputs and outputs. A tool with `needsApproval: true` causes registration to fail.\n\n### Public option types\n\n- `RegisterWebMCPToolsOptions<TTools, TContext>` - Requires `signal`. It also contains `toolOptions` and the client tool runtime `context`.\n- `WebMCPToolOptionsByName<TTools>` - A partial options map keyed by the inferred tool names.\n- `WebMCPToolOptions` - Contains the optional `title` and `annotations` fields for one tool.\n- `WebMCPToolAnnotations` - Contains the optional `readOnlyHint` and `untrustedContentHint` fields.\n\n`context` is required when a tool declares a required runtime context. If registration fails, the function removes tools that it registered during the call.\n\n## `ChatClient`\n\nThe main client class for managing chat state.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  ChatClient,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type UIMessage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { myClientTool } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  initialMessages: [],\n  tools: [myClientTool],\n  onMessagesChange: (messages: UIMessage[]) => {\n    console.log(\"Messages updated:\", messages);\n  },\n});\n\n// A new client is IDLE. Attach it when your view appears, detach when it goes.\nclient.attach();\n```\n\n### Lifecycle: `attach()` and `detach()`\n\nOne page can hold many chats. A browser allows only about six connections to one\norigin, and a chat that is tailing a run holds one for as long as that run lasts. If\nevery chat held a connection, a handful of open views would use every slot and every\nother request would queue behind them, including the request that loads your messages.\n\nSo the connection follows the view. A new client holds none, `attach()` starts it, and\n`detach()` stops it.\n\nIf you use a framework package (`@tanstack/ai-react`, `-vue`, `-solid`, `-svelte`,\n`-preact`, `-angular`), the hook already does this: it attaches when its view mounts\nand detaches when it unmounts. Call these yourself only when you use `ChatClient`\ndirectly.\n\n```typescript\nimport { ChatClient, fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  threadId: \"thread-1\",\n  persistence: true,\n});\n\nclient.attach(); // start: rejoin a run in progress, and load the thread\nclient.detach(); // stop: drop the connection, keep messages and the run pointer\n```\n\nWhat each one guarantees:\n\n- `attach()` is safe to call more than once. Attaching an attached client does nothing.\n- `detach()` keeps the transcript, the resume pointer and the run id. The run keeps\n  going on the server while nobody watches, so re-attaching repaints at once and picks\n  it back up from the durable log.\n- `detach()` is neither `stop()` (which ends the run) nor `dispose()` (which ends the\n  client). It says only that no view is watching right now.\n- A chat with no persistence has no resume pointer and no stored thread, so `attach()`\n  issues no request at all.\n\n#### Migrating from constructor tailing\n\nEarlier versions started tailing inside the constructor. If you build a `ChatClient`\nyourself, add `client.attach()` where your view appears and `client.detach()` where it\ngoes away. Users of the framework hooks need no change.\n\n### Constructor Options\n\n- `connection` - Connection adapter for streaming\n- `initialMessages?` - Initial messages array\n- `threadId?` - The only identity for this chat. Required when persistence is on. If omitted, minted after mount.\n- `forwardedProps?` - Arbitrary client-controlled JSON forwarded to the server in the AG-UI `RunAgentInput.forwardedProps` field\n- `body?` - **Deprecated.** Use `forwardedProps` instead. Still works — values are merged into `forwardedProps` on the wire and mirrored under the legacy `data` field for backward compatibility\n- `byok?` - Optional BYOK keyring from [`defineByok`](#definebyok). On each send the client prepares the resolved provider and stamps `x-byok-*` request headers. Keys never go in the body\n- `byokProvider?` - Optional function that returns the provider slug for this chat. If it returns a slug, only that key is prepared and sent. Otherwise the merged `provider` from `forwardedProps`, `body`, and per-call `sendMessage` `body` is used. Later sources win. If no slug resolves, the send throws instead of attaching every stored key\n- `context?` - Typed client-local runtime context passed to client tool implementations. This value is not serialized to the server\n- `tools?` - Registered `.client()` tool implementations. The client automatically executes matching tools when the model calls them\n- `onResponse?` - Callback when response is received\n- `onChunk?` - Callback when stream chunk is received\n- `onFinish?` - Callback when response finishes\n- `onError?` - Callback when error occurs\n- `onInterruptStateChange?` - Callback when interrupt state changes; context source is `hydrate` for restored state and `live` for streamed or client-initiated updates\n- `onMessagesChange?` - Callback when messages change\n- `onLoadingChange?` - Callback when loading state changes\n- `onHydratingChange?` - Callback when the client starts or stops loading the chat from persistence\n- `onErrorChange?` - Callback when error state changes\n- `streamProcessor?` - Stream processing configuration\n\n### Methods\n\n#### `sendMessage(content: string | MultimodalContent, body?, sendOptions?)`\n\nSends a user message and starts the run.\n\n`MultimodalContent` is `{ content, id?, metadata? }`. The string form has no metadata. Pass the object form to stamp `metadata` on the user `UIMessage`. TanStack writes the `tanstack` key. Your keys stay at the top of the bag.\n\nThe second argument is extra JSON merged into this request's `forwardedProps`. The third argument is `SendMessageOptions`. `{ whenBusy }` overrides the queue policy for this send. `{ body }` is extra JSON too.\n\nChat-level `body`, the positional argument, and `sendOptions.body` shallow-merge. `sendOptions.body` wins on key collisions.\n\nFramework hooks expose `sendMessage(content, sendOptions)` with no positional body. Pass `{ body }` there. It merges with the hook's `body` the same way.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.sendMessage(\"Hello!\");\n\nawait client.sendMessage({\n  content: \"Show me failed logins\",\n  metadata: { author: { id: \"user-42\", name: \"Dana\" } },\n});\n\nawait client.sendMessage(\"Summarize the attached files\", undefined, {\n  body: { attachmentIds: [\"att_1\", \"att_2\"] },\n  whenBusy: \"interrupt\",\n});\n```\n\nYour server reads the merged JSON from `chatParamsFromRequest`:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { openaiText } from \"@tanstack/ai-openai\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages, forwardedProps } = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(\"gpt-5.5\"),\n    messages,\n  });\n  if (\n    forwardedProps &&\n    typeof forwardedProps === \"object\" &&\n    \"attachmentIds\" in forwardedProps\n  ) {\n    const { attachmentIds } = forwardedProps;\n    if (Array.isArray(attachmentIds) && attachmentIds.length > 0) {\n      // Look up the uploads. Do not add them to `messages`.\n    }\n  }\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\n#### `append(message: ModelMessage | UIMessage)`\n\nAppends a message to the conversation. If you pass a `UIMessage`, `append` copies `uiMessage.metadata` onto the stored message.\n\n`append()` resolves after the full HTTP response is processed when this call starts the stream. If a stream is already in progress, this call queues the send and the returned promise can resolve before that queued response is processed. A `RUN_FINISHED` with `finishReason: \"tool_calls\"` does not end the wait when the agent loop continues in that response.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\nimport type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nawait client.append({\n  role: \"user\",\n  content: \"Additional context\",\n});\n\nconst stamped: UIMessage = {\n  id: \"user-1\",\n  role: \"user\",\n  parts: [{ type: \"text\", content: \"Show me failed logins\" }],\n  metadata: { author: { id: \"user-42\", name: \"Dana\" } },\n};\nawait client.append(stamped);\n```\n\n#### `reload()`\n\nReloads the last assistant message.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.reload();\n```\n\n#### `attach()`\n\nStart tailing. Rejoins a run that is still in progress and, in server-authoritative\nmode, loads the stored thread. Idempotent. See\n[Lifecycle](#lifecycle-attach-and-detach).\n\n#### `detach()`\n\nStop tailing and drop the connection. Keeps messages, the run pointer and the run\nid, so a later `attach()` continues where it left off. See\n[Lifecycle](#lifecycle-attach-and-detach).\n\n#### `stop()`\n\nStops the current response generation. It aborts the in-flight request.\nPending client-tool results for that turn are ignored. A later\n`addToolResult()` call for that turn is ignored. It does not start a resume.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nclient.stop();\n```\n\n#### `clear()`\n\nClears all messages.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nclient.clear();\n```\n\n#### `setMessagesManually(messages: UIMessage[])`\n\nManually sets the messages array.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\nimport type { UIMessage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst newMessages: UIMessage[] = [];\nclient.setMessagesManually([...newMessages]);\n```\n\n#### `addToolResult(result)`\n\nAdds the result of a client-side tool execution. After `stop()`, a result for\nthe stopped turn is ignored. A new user message starts a new turn. Then\n`addToolResult()` applies to that turn.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.addToolResult({\n  toolCallId: \"call_123\",\n  tool: \"toolName\",\n  output: { result: \"...\" },\n  state: \"output-available\",\n});\n```\n\n#### `addToolApprovalResponse(response)`\n\nResponds to a tool approval request.\n\n```typescript\nimport { client } from \"./client\";\n\nawait client.addToolApprovalResponse({\n  id: \"approval_123\",\n  approved: true,\n});\n```\n\n### Properties\n\n- `messages: UIMessage[]` - Current messages\n- `isLoading: boolean` - Whether a response is being generated\n- `isHydrating: boolean` - Whether the chat is loading from persistence. Read it with `getIsHydrating()`\n- `error: Error | undefined` - Current error, if any\n\n## Connection Adapters\n\nFor a complete transport walkthrough, see\n[Transports](../transports/overview). For React Native and Expo,\nsee [React Native](../transports/react-native) and\n[Quick Start: React Native](../getting-started/quick-start-react-native).\n\n### `fetchServerSentEvents(url, options?)`\n\nCreates an SSE connection adapter.\n\n```typescript\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\", {\n  headers: {\n    Authorization: \"Bearer token\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### `fetchHttpStream(url, options?)`\n\nCreates a newline-delimited JSON HTTP stream connection adapter. Pair it with\n`toHttpResponse()` on the server.\n\n```typescript\nimport { fetchHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchHttpStream(\"/api/chat\");\n```\n\n`fetchHttpStream()` requires a runtime with streaming `fetch`,\n`Response.body.getReader()`, and `TextDecoder`. If the runtime cannot expose an\nincremental response body, it throws `UnsupportedResponseStreamError`; use the\nXHR adapters in React Native or Expo.\n\n### `fetchJson(url, options?)`\n\nCreates a connection adapter for one JSON body per request. Pair it with\n`toJsonResponse()` on the server. It does not need a streaming response body.\n\n```typescript\nimport { fetchJson } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = fetchJson(\"/api/chat\", {\n  pollIntervalMs: 500,\n});\n```\n\nIt takes the fetch adapter options, plus `pollIntervalMs` (default 250). When a\nreply has `done: false`, the adapter waits `pollIntervalMs` and sends\n`GET ?runId=<id>&offset=<offset>`. Serve that `GET` with `resumeJsonResponse()`.\nSee [JSON](../transports/json).\n\n### `xhrHttpStream(url, options?)`\n\nCreates an `XMLHttpRequest`-backed newline-delimited JSON stream adapter. This\nis the recommended default for React Native and Expo chat screens. Pair it with\n`toHttpResponse()` on the server.\n\n```typescript\nimport { xhrHttpStream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = xhrHttpStream(\"http://192.168.1.10:8787/chat/http\", {\n  headers: { Authorization: \"Bearer token\" },\n  withCredentials: true,\n});\n```\n\n### `xhrServerSentEvents(url, options?)`\n\nCreates an `XMLHttpRequest`-backed SSE adapter for runtimes where XHR progress\nevents are more reliable than streaming `fetch`. Pair it with\n`toServerSentEventsResponse()` on the server.\n\n```typescript\nimport { xhrServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = xhrServerSentEvents(\"http://192.168.1.10:8787/chat/sse\");\n```\n\n### Adapter options\n\nFetch adapters accept:\n\n- `headers?: Record<string, string> | Headers`\n- `credentials?: RequestCredentials`\n- `signal?: AbortSignal`\n- `body?: Record<string, any>`\n- `fetchClient?: typeof globalThis.fetch`\n\nXHR adapters accept:\n\n- `headers?: Record<string, string> | Headers`\n- `withCredentials?: boolean`\n- `signal?: AbortSignal`\n- `body?: Record<string, any>`\n- `xhrFactory?: () => XMLHttpRequest`\n\n`body` is merged into the AG-UI `forwardedProps` payload. Values from\n`forwardedProps` on the client and per-message `sendMessage` `body` (positional\nor `sendOptions.body`) override static adapter `body` values.\n\n### Stream errors\n\n- `UnsupportedResponseStreamError` - thrown by fetch-based adapters when\n  `Response.body`, `Response.body.getReader()`, or `TextDecoder` is missing.\n- `StreamTruncatedError` - thrown when an SSE or NDJSON stream ends with\n  unterminated trailing data, usually because the server, proxy, or network cut\n  the connection mid-line.\n\n### `stream(connectFn)`\n\nCreates a custom connection adapter.\n\n```typescript ignore\nimport { stream } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst adapter = stream(async (messages, data, signal) => {\n  // `data` here carries the merged forwardedProps. The fetch-based\n  // adapters serialize it as the AG-UI `RunAgentInput.forwardedProps`\n  // field on the wire (with a backward-compat `data` mirror).\n  const response = await fetch(\"/api/chat\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    body: JSON.stringify({ messages, forwardedProps: data }),\n    signal,\n  });\n  return processStream(response);\n});\n```\n\n## Helper Functions\n\n### `clientTools(...tools)`\n\n**Optional.** A plain array — `tools: [tool1, tool2]` — already narrows tool names, inputs and outputs without any wrapper or `as const`. `clientTools()` is an identity helper that performs the same capture explicitly; reach for it only when you want to build a shared, reusable tools tuple outside the hook/options call.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  clientTools,\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type UIMessage,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst messages: UIMessage[] = [];\n\nconst myTool1 = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"myTool1\",\n  description: \"First tool\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ result: z.string() }),\n});\n\nconst myTool2 = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"myTool2\",\n  description: \"Second tool\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ query: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ result: z.string() }),\n});\n\n// Create client implementations\nconst tool1Client = myTool1.client((input) => {\n  // Implementation\n  return { result: input.query };\n});\n\nconst tool2Client = myTool2.client((input) => {\n  // Implementation\n  return { result: input.query };\n});\n\n// The explicit-capture form (equivalent to `[tool1Client, tool2Client]`).\nconst tools = clientTools(tool1Client, tool2Client);\n\n// Now when you use these tools in chat options:\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools, // Fully typed with literal tool names\n});\n\n// In your component:\nmessages.forEach((message) => {\n  message.parts.forEach((part) => {\n    if (part.type === \"tool-call\" && part.name === \"myTool1\") {\n      // ✅ TypeScript knows part.name is literally \"myTool1\"\n      // ✅ part.input is typed from myTool1's input schema\n      // ✅ part.output is typed from myTool1's output schema\n    }\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `createChatClientOptions(options)`\n\nHelper function to create typed chat client options with proper type inference.\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n  type InferChatMessages,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { tool1, tool2 } from \"./tools\";\n\nconst tools = [tool1, tool2];\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools,\n});\n\n// Use InferChatMessages to extract message types\ntype ChatMessages = InferChatMessages<typeof chatOptions>;\n```\n\n`createChatClientOptions` also preserves typed client runtime context:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  createChatClientOptions,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\nimport { toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\n\ntype ClientContext = {\n  activeProjectId: string;\n};\n\nconst projectTool = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"projectAction\",\n  description: \"Run a project action\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ action: z.string() }),\n  outputSchema: z.object({ ok: z.boolean() }),\n});\n\nconst tool = projectTool.client<ClientContext>((input, ctx: { context: ClientContext }) => {\n  console.log(ctx.context.activeProjectId, input.action);\n  return { ok: true };\n});\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatClientOptions({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  tools: [tool],\n  context: {\n    activeProjectId: \"project_123\",\n  },\n});\n```\n\nClient runtime context is local to the client instance. Use `forwardedProps` for explicit client-to-server handoff of serializable values, then validate and map those values into server `chat({ context })`.\n\n## `defineByok`\n\nFactory for a headless BYOK keyring. Import it from `@tanstack/ai-client/byok`. Pass the instance into `ChatClient`, `useChat`, or a generation hook. See [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) for a full client and relay walkthrough.\n\n```typescript\nimport { defineByok, defaultByokStorage } from \"@tanstack/ai-client/byok\";\n\nexport const byok = defineByok({\n  storage: defaultByokStorage(),\n});\n```\n\n### Factory options\n\n- `storage?` - A `KeyringStorage` implementation. Default is `memoryStorage()` (session only, not saved)\n- `providers?` - Descriptors whose `with` companions the store expands. With `[cloudflareByok, cloudflareAccountByok]`, a send for `cloudflare` carries the token and the account id headers, and `prepare` prompts for each missing one\n\n### Methods\n\n- `update(provider, key)` - Persist a key for a provider slug (`[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,63}`), then update the snapshot. Throws if the id is not a slug, the key is empty, or storage fails\n- `update(key)` - Persist a key for the current `prompt` provider. Throws if `prompt` is null\n- `clear(provider?)` - Persist the removal, then drop one key, or all keys when you omit `provider`\n- `unlock()` - Decrypt unlockable storage (passkey). No-op for memory storage\n- `headers(provider)` - Return `x-byok-*` headers for that slug and its companions. Chat and generation clients throw if no slug resolves — they do not send every stored key\n- `prepare(provider?)` - Wait for hydration, then unlock if needed. If `provider` is set and the key for it or a companion is empty with no server coverage, throw `ByokBlockedError` and set `prompt` for that slug\n- `ready()` - Resolve when constructor hydration (peek/load) finishes\n- `setServerCoverage(flags)` - `true` means do not block a send when the browser has no key (the relay can fill from env). `false` restores the default: block. A record merges per-slug flags\n- `request(provider, reason)` - Set `prompt` to `{ provider, reason }` (`missing` | `locked` | `invalid`)\n- `getSnapshot()` - Return the current [`ByokSnapshot`](#snapshot)\n- `subscribe(listener)` - Call `listener` on each change. Returns an unsubscribe function\n- `keys()` - Return a copy of the raw keyring. Do not render this in the UI\n\n### Snapshot\n\n`getSnapshot()` (and framework readers such as `useByok`) return:\n\n```typescript ignore\ntype ByokSnapshot = {\n  status: Partial<Record<string, KeyStatus>>;\n  locked: boolean;\n  prompt: { provider: string; reason: \"missing\" | \"locked\" | \"invalid\" } | null;\n  storageError: string | null;\n};\n\ntype KeyStatus =\n  | { state: \"empty\" }\n  | { state: \"set\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"locked\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"validating\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"valid\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"invalid\"; masked: string }\n  | { state: \"error\"; masked: string; message: string };\n```\n\n`status` is sparse: only slugs that have a key, a lock, or a validation result appear. A missing entry means no key. `masked` is the last four characters of the key (`maskKey`). Read it with `\"masked\" in status` — `{ state: \"empty\" }` has no `masked`. `storageError` is set when peek/load fails. The snapshot never includes the raw key.\n\n### Storage\n\n- `defaultByokStorage(options?)` - Passkey-encrypted IndexedDB when WebAuthn is available in a secure context. Otherwise `memoryStorage()` with a warning. WebAuthn support is not the same as PRF — first save still throws if the authenticator lacks PRF\n- `memoryStorage()` - In-memory on the `ByokClient` instance. This backend does not persist. Keys are gone when the client is dropped or the page reloads\n- `passkeyStorage(options?)` - Encrypt the keyring with a WebAuthn passkey. First save throws if the authenticator does not support PRF\n- `KeyringStorage` - `{ id, label, persistent, unlockable?, peek?, load, save, clear }`\n\nThis library does not ship a dialog. Call `byok.update(provider, value)` from your own UI.\n\n## Types\n\n### `UIMessage`\n\n```typescript ignore\ninterface UIMessage {\n  id: string;\n  role: \"system\" | \"user\" | \"assistant\";\n  parts: MessagePart[];\n  name?: string;\n  createdAt?: Date;\n  metadata?: Record<string, any>;\n}\n```\n\n`metadata` is an optional AG-UI bag (`Record<string, any>`). TanStack writes the `tanstack` key. Your keys stay at the top.\n\n### `MessagePart`\n\n```typescript ignore\ntype MessagePart = TextPart | ThinkingPart | ToolCallPart | ToolResultPart;\n```\n\n### `TextPart`\n\n```typescript\ninterface TextPart {\n  type: \"text\";\n  content: string;\n}\n```\n\n### `ThinkingPart`\n\n```typescript\ninterface ThinkingPart {\n  type: \"thinking\";\n  content: string;\n}\n```\n\nThinking parts represent the model's internal reasoning process. They are typically displayed in a collapsible format and automatically collapse when the response text appears. Thinking parts are UI-only and are not sent back to the model in subsequent requests.\n\n**Note:** Thinking parts are only available when using models that support reasoning/thinking (e.g., Anthropic Claude with thinking enabled, OpenAI GPT-5 with reasoning enabled).\n\n### `ToolCallPart`\n\n```typescript ignore\ninterface ToolCallPart {\n  type: \"tool-call\";\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  arguments: string; // JSON string (may be incomplete during streaming)\n  input?: any; // Parsed tool input (typed from tool's inputSchema)\n  state: ToolCallState;\n  approval?: ApprovalRequest; // only on tools declared `needsApproval: true`\n  output?: any; // Tool execution output (typed from tool's outputSchema)\n}\n```\n\nWhen you pass a typed `tools` array (a plain array works — `clientTools()` is optional), the `input` and `output` fields are automatically typed based on your tool's Zod schemas, and `name` becomes a discriminated union enabling type narrowing. The `approval` field is present **only** on parts for tools declared with `needsApproval: true` — narrow by `part.name` (or guard with `'approval' in part`) before accessing it.\n\n### `ToolResultPart`\n\n```typescript ignore\ninterface ToolResultPart {\n  type: \"tool-result\";\n  id?: string;\n  name?: string;\n  toolCallId: string;\n  content: string | ContentPart[];\n  state: ToolResultState;\n  error?: string;\n  metadata?: Record<string, unknown>;\n  createdAt?: Date;\n}\n```\n\n### `ToolCallState`\n\n```typescript ignore\ntype ToolCallState =\n  | \"awaiting-input\"\n  | \"input-streaming\"\n  | \"input-complete\"\n  | \"approval-requested\"\n  | \"approval-responded\"\n  | \"complete\";\n```\n\n### `ToolResultState`\n\n```typescript ignore\ntype ToolResultState =\n  | \"streaming\"\n  | \"complete\"\n  | \"error\";\n```\n\n## Stream Processing\n\nConfigure stream processing with chunk strategies:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  ChatClient,\n  ImmediateStrategy,\n  fetchServerSentEvents,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nconst client = new ChatClient({\n  connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\"),\n  streamProcessor: {\n    chunkStrategy: new ImmediateStrategy(), // Emit every chunk\n  },\n});\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- [Getting Started](../getting-started/quick-start) - Learn the basics\n- [Bring Your Own Key](../advanced/byok) - Store keys in the browser and send `x-byok-*` headers\n- [Transports](../transports/overview) - Learn about adapters\n- [@tanstack/ai-react API](./ai-react) - React hooks wrapper\n"}
